{
  "regeln": [
    "Match visuals directly to the specific business action, transaction figure, or legal instrument narrated—displaying period contracts, financial ledgers, disputed signatures, or relevant artifacts rather than generic street scenes, metaphorical poses, or crowd filler.",
    "Center scripts strictly on leadership rivalries, equity disputes, and control transitions, eliminating commercial marketing trivia, consumer packaging milestones, and thematic digressions that do not answer the central conflict.",
    "Open with a compelling visual hook that articulates the central corporate conflict and its core dilemma in exactly one concise, unified question.",
    "Verify all historical dates, corporate titles, transaction amounts, and legal transitions strictly against source records, eliminating anachronistic or future dates.",
    "Align environmental details, architecture, props, and wardrobe strictly with the specific historical era and geographical setting cited in the narration.",
    "Depict historical participants using era-appropriate role archetypes without reproducing real-life facial likenesses, living portraits, or commercial brand logos.",
    "Feature distinct visual settings and staged interactions for competing founders, executives, and investors to clearly convey shifting power dynamics.",
    "Emphasize high-stakes financial crises, near-bankruptcy risks, and structural contract vulnerabilities to preserve dramatic tension rather than portraying smooth growth.",
    "Adapt narrative depth and visual rhythm strictly to the chosen format, keeping Shorts focused on rapid conflict beats while allowing deliberate scene progression in long-form videos."
  ],
